<title>GERMANY: Bonn to top up Series 120 Bobls by 1 bln marks.</title>
<headline>Bonn to top up Series 120 Bobls by 1 bln marks.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government will top up the issue of its Series 120 Bundesobligationen bonds, or Bobls, by one billion marks to nine billion marks, the Bundesbank as issuing agent said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The new tranche will be issued as part of the Bundesbank's market-smoothing operations from December 27 onwards, the Bundesbank said.</p>
<p>The paper matures on August 20, 2001.</p>
<p>On Thursday the paper yielded 4.57 percent for a price of 101.74.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
